#!/bin/sh
# lawha launcher. Skills and agents call it as "lawha <command>"; see `lawha help`.
#   lawha setup                  install the engine (Playwright + Chromium) once, outside the project
#   lawha hook session-start     the short note Claude gets at the start of a session (only with a frontend)
#   lawha has-frontend [dir]     "yes" (exit 0) when the project has a frontend, else "no" (exit 1)
#   lawha <engine command> ...   check, diff, index, version (run by the engine)
set -eu

here=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
src="$here/engine"
version=$(sed -n 's/^  "version": "\(.*\)",$/\1/p' "$src/package.json")
home="${LAWHA_HOME:-$HOME/.claude/nexika/lawha}"
installed="$home/engine/$version"

engine_dir() {
  if [ -n "${LAWHA_ENGINE:-}" ]; then echo "$LAWHA_ENGINE"; return; fi
  if [ -d "$src/node_modules/playwright" ]; then echo "$src"; return; fi       # developing lawha itself
  if [ -d "$installed/node_modules/playwright" ]; then echo "$installed"; return; fi
  echo ""
}

# Does the project have a frontend? Looks at the folder and one level down (apps/* and packages/*
# two levels down) for a package.json that names a UI library, a frontend config file, or lawha's
# own .lawha folder. Only file tests and a grep per package.json: fast, and any error means "no".
FRONTEND_DEPS='"(react|react-dom|vue|svelte|@sveltejs/kit|next|nuxt|astro|@angular/core|solid-js|preact|lit|@remix-run/react|@tanstack/react-router|tailwindcss)"[[:space:]]*:'
FRONTEND_FILES="tailwind.config.js tailwind.config.ts tailwind.config.mjs tailwind.config.cjs components.json
  vite.config.js vite.config.ts vite.config.mjs next.config.js next.config.mjs next.config.ts nuxt.config.ts
  nuxt.config.js astro.config.mjs astro.config.ts svelte.config.js angular.json index.html public/index.html
  src/index.html"

looks_like_frontend() {
  [ -d "$1" ] || return 1
  for f in $FRONTEND_FILES; do
    [ -f "$1/$f" ] && return 0
  done
  [ -f "$1/package.json" ] && grep -Eq "$FRONTEND_DEPS" "$1/package.json" 2>/dev/null && return 0
  return 1
}

has_frontend() {
  root=$1
  [ -d "$root" ] || return 1
  [ -d "$root/.lawha" ] && return 0
  looks_like_frontend "$root" && return 0
  for d in "$root"/*/ "$root"/apps/*/ "$root"/packages/*/; do
    d=${d%/}
    case "${d##*/}" in node_modules|vendor|dist|build|htmlcov|coverage|site-packages) continue ;; esac
    looks_like_frontend "$d" && return 0
  done
  return 1
}

case "${1:-help}" in
  has-frontend)
    if has_frontend "${2:-${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}}"; then echo yes; else echo no; exit 1; fi
    ;;
  setup)
    command -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo '{"error": "Node.js 20 or newer is needed: https://nodejs.org"}'; exit 3; }
    major=$(node -p 'process.versions.node.split(".")[0]')
    [ "$major" -ge 20 ] || { echo "{\"error\": \"Node.js $major is too old; lawha needs 20 or newer\"}"; exit 3; }
    mkdir -p "$installed/dist"
    cp "$src/package.json" "$src/package-lock.json" "$installed/"
    cp -R "$src/dist/." "$installed/dist/"
    (cd "$installed" && npm ci --omit=dev --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error >&2 \
      && node node_modules/playwright/cli.js install chromium >&2)
    cat "$src"/dist/*.js | cksum > "$installed/.dist-sum"
    echo "{\"installed\": \"$installed\", \"version\": \"$version\"}"
    ;;
  hook)
    [ "${NEXIKA_BACKGROUND:-}" = "1" ] && exit 0  # inside a family background model call: no hooks (#45)
    # Quiet in a project with no frontend (#336): the skills still work, they find the helper themselves.
    has_frontend "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}" || exit 0
    if [ -n "$(engine_dir)" ]; then state="ready"; else state="not installed (run: lawha setup, after asking the user)"; fi
    echo "lawha: frontend design, Figma to code and checks on every screen. Helper: $here/bin/lawha · engine $version $state."
    ;;
  *)
    dir=$(engine_dir)
    # An installed engine follows the plugin's code: a plugin update with the same version must not
    # leave an old engine running. New code is copied in; new dependencies need `lawha setup` again.
    if [ -n "$dir" ] && [ "$dir" = "$installed" ]; then
      if ! cmp -s "$src/package-lock.json" "$installed/package-lock.json"; then
        echo "{\"error\": \"lawha's engine dependencies changed\", \"fix\": \"$here/bin/lawha setup\"}"
        exit 3
      fi
      sum=$(cat "$src"/dist/*.js | cksum)
      if [ "$sum" != "$(cat "$installed/.dist-sum" 2>/dev/null)" ]; then
        cp -R "$src/dist/." "$installed/dist/" && cp "$src/package.json" "$installed/" && echo "$sum" > "$installed/.dist-sum"
      fi
    fi
    if [ -z "$dir" ]; then
      echo "{\"error\": \"lawha's engine is not installed\", \"fix\": \"$here/bin/lawha setup\", \"needs\": \"Node.js 20+, about 300 MB for Chromium, installed in $installed (nothing is added to the project)\"}"
      exit 3
    fi
    exec node "$dir/dist/cli.js" "$@"
    ;;
esac
